- The only unreachable targets from Location C are **172.18.50.x/172.18.51.x** (Location B behind router6), but router6 has a FORWARD-chain DROP policy for all traffic arriving on eth2 (the upstream interface) — this is the known baseline "B→A" security policy that has always been present, not an injected fault

